# --- build output ---
/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage/

# --- generated frontend bundle ---
# `npm run build` writes vite's outDir here, and the server embeds that directory
# as an assembly resource. It is a build artifact rather than a source file, so
# it is not committed: run `npm run build` (or `make build`) before publishing
# the server, or the published image has no console in it.
/web/dist/
/web/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- editors and OS noise ---
.vscode/
.idea/
# Visual Studio's own state: solution caches, .suo, Copilot symbol databases and
# test logs. Regenerated on open, so it is never worth committing.
.vs/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- local overrides ---
.env
.env.*
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- .NET build output (dotnet/) ---
# These have to be spelled out: every rule above is anchored to the repository
# root, so `/bin/` does not reach into dotnet/, and nothing here covers `obj/`
# at all. Without them `dotnet/**/obj/project.assets.json` and the compiled
# assemblies are untracked-but-addable build output.
dotnet/**/bin/
dotnet/**/obj/
*.user
